A||||8||BBBAD GT||Vac Line Help||||1||
Z||000000||BBBAD GT||02-16-2000||09:25 AM||||<BR>I can't figure this one out, and need some help (or another v6 to look at).  I noticed a rubber line hose going from the air cleaner (in the back of the canister) to a hard line that runs the side of the firewall, then into another rubber line that just stops.  It looks like it should be connected somewhere along the firewall side of the manifold, but can't find a lead that is open (this line is pretty big, could stick my pinky through it).  I've looked through the service manual, and its not the pcv line, or the other vac line that run through the middle of the firewall.  I have no driveability problems, and I'm thinking if one side is hooked to the air canister, then it should be a pcv thing, but its not.  Anybody got any suggestions? Sure wish I had another v6 to look at.  <P> <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/fiero1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/fiero1.jpg</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||RICK||02-16-2000||10:52 AM||||I don't think I live that far away, if you want to meet this weekend somewhere you can take a look at mine.  (87 V6, SE 5sp)||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||02-16-2000||12:09 PM||||I just went out and followed that line on my Fiero. It plus onto the EGR solonoid. Sounds like someone put the wrong diameter hose on though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTBro||02-16-2000||12:13 PM||||Some people say it is not necessary to have that line connected to the EGR solenoid.  I have mine connected though.  It is supposed to go there, but it doesn't have to be.||||reg||1
Z||000004||daved||02-16-2000||12:20 PM||||Mine has that same pipe...abandonded after one of the recalls.  But the pipe to the air cleaner was supposed to be plugged, provided by GM with the recall kit. (Mine was missing and was allowing dirty air into the engine! ) For some reason, the GM recall had instructions to leave the pipe attached to the firewall...cant see why though.  Anybody taken it off as its an eyesore?||||reg||1
Z||000005||BBBAD GT||02-16-2000||12:46 PM||||I feel better now.  I really didn't think it did much, because my drivability wasn't suffering a bit (well, not too bad).  I guess I'll plug it up or take it off entirely. Am I to assume during the recall, the EGR was replaced, and the port opening was no longer there?  Thanks for the input.<P> ||||reg||7
Z||000006||DRH||02-16-2000||02:26 PM||||The tube affected by the recalls is a larger tube that ends near the center of the engine bay. The tube for the EGR solenoid is smaller and ends closer to the passenger side.<P>Basically the recall re-routed the crankcase vent tube on the rear valve cover from the air cleaner assy to the inlet tube for the throttle body. See the attached link for the recall complete with pictures.<P> <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/v6recall.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/v6recall.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||02-16-2000||02:31 PM||||Looks like I was looking at the wrong line. The one you were talking about is supposed to be blocked off. On mine the pipe is still there, but is no longer connected to anything, and the hole on the filter canister is plugged.||||reg||1
Z||000008||BBBAD GT||02-16-2000||04:43 PM||||Thanks DRH for clearing it up.  I've actually printed out that Dealer Product Campaign, but haven't read it yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Also thanks for offering your v6 for a looksey Rick.<P><BR>||||reg||1
